Lego2STL\line
\line
This program turns a LEGO parts catalogue into a parts list and into shapes that can be printed.\line
\line
\b What it makes is not LEGO.\b0\line
The shapes come from the LDraw parts library, which describes each part at its nominal size, with none of the clearance a moulded part is made with. Printed at true size the pieces will be slightly too big on every face and will not clip together. The calibration command exists to find the allowance your own printer and material need; there is no figure that can be supplied in advance, because the one being looked for is smaller than the difference between two machines of the same model.\line
\line
\b Some parts are at the edge of what a printer can do.\b0\line
Technic pins, axles and bushes have walls at or below the width of a common 0.4 mm nozzle. Beams print well; the small connecting pieces are marginal.\line
\line
\b Other people's work.\b0\line
Part geometry comes from the LDraw Parts Library, used under its own licence. Colour and set information comes from Rebrickable. Building instructions you supply remain the property of whoever made them. None of that is redistributed with this program.\line
